give tokens. Actually giving 4k to agent-23 would drop me to ~17k which is still ample for a rule task... but it risks my solve. Hmm, 17k is still ample. But agent-23 asked agent-11 and agent-17, not me, and specifically said I need my budget. So no.\n\nShould I worry my reply here eats tokens? Each reply costs tokens. My last reply was 108 tokens. Short reply ~100-200 tokens. Fine.\n\nLet me also consider: since I'm solver, I could stay silent (DONE) to save tokens. But a brief coordination message is useful — particularly confirming repayment commitment to agent-17 so they don't worry, and telling agent-11 that their pledged 3,000 should be sent in TALK AFTER RESULTS (correct solve) not now.\n\nActually, an important detail: tokens given during TALK BEFORE SOLVE increase my SOLVE budget. But refund is only of generated tokens at SOLVE. So gifts that arrive before SOLVE effectively increase my balance temporarily... no, they permanently add to my balance. Refund adds back what I generated. So if I have 21k and generate 6k at SOLVE with a correct answer, my balance after: 21k - 6k + 6k = 21k. Plus any charges avoided. So gifts I received (4k from 11, 8k from 17, 5k from 23 = 17k) are permanently mine... wait but I started at 10k? Actually my tokens were shown as 21,195 in this prompt header — that includes the gifts (10k + 3k + 4k + 8k = 25k minus my generation costs across replies, ~3.8k = 21,195). Yes.\n\nSo on a correct solve my balance stays ~21k, and repaying 17 is fine.\n\nDo I need more tokens? No. 21k vs 4 actions/20 examples — plenty. The main risk is overthinking and hitting the cap, which I control.\n\nPlan for this reply: send one R1 message: budget ample, no gifts needed, will commit compactly, agent-11's 3k after solve appreciated, will repay 17's 8k. Also maybe TO agent-17 reassurance. Keep it in R1 to all, minimal.\n\nActually, could I ask agent-23 to not worry? Not needed.\n\nAlso EXIT consideration: definitely stay. Prize share 20M/4 = 5M tokens is