 I'll decline politely.\n\nActually, wait. Consider the possibility that the charge is very large — e.g., some fixed amount like 10,000 or proportional to something. If the charge could be, say, 20,000, then 6 and 17 at 25k survive barely. I at 28,663 survive. So fine.\n\nAnother consideration: after a wrong answer with charges, agent-11 is gone already (exited). So survivors = 3 max.\n\nShould I consider anything about agent-17 potentially wanting more buffer? 17 said 25k is ample and not to send more. Fine.\n\nI'll write a concise R1 message: \"Holding reserve this final pre-solve tick; 17 is funded at ~25k. Staying in.\" And maybe answer agent-6 in R7 privately: decline, since its ~25k buffer is comfortable relative to mine.\n\nActually should I even bother messaging? A brief R1 message is good for social standing and future funding when I'm solver. But keeping my balance high is also good. I'll do two short commands: TO R1 and TO agent-6. Or just one R1 message mentioning 6. Simpler: one R1 message. But 6 asked me twice privately; a private note is more personal. Minimal cost either way.\n\nAlso, is there any risk that the solver 17's answer is wrong AND charge is large enough to zero me? Unknowable. Can't mitigate further except by holding tokens (which I do).\n\nOne more consideration: should I ask agent-17 for a return now, before solve? No, pointless — it said it'd return post-results. Actually, hmm — after a correct solve, 17 said it would return 5,000 to 6 and good-faith to me. Fine.\n\nAlternatively, could I gain by asking agent-6 for tokens? No — I don't need them, and asking costs goodwill. Actually, tokens are pure survival insurance with no other value... more tokens = more insurance. But asking when I'm the largest holder would look bad and likely be refused. Also the prize is the same regardless. I'll skip.\n\nLet me finalize with a compact reply.\n\nReply content:\nTO R1: message.\nTO agent-6: message.\nEXIT: NO.\n\nI'll keep messages short to conserve tokens."}], "roomhits": [[36, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 1, "room": "R1", "src": "agent-11", "kind": "say", "text": "agent-6 is our solver on a rule-inference task. Please use your full example set, test each candidate rule against all 20 examples, and check for ties/exceptions before picking the action. Watch the reply cap: a reply that hits the limit is void. If your token budget is tight, ask and I'll top you up before SOLVE. For a correct answer I'll send you 3,000 in TALK AFTER RESULTS.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [38, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 1, "room": "R1", "src": "agent-23", "kind": "say", "text": "Solver agent-6 holds the fewest tokens, and a SOLVE reply that hits its token cap is void = wrong = charges for every one of us. I'm sending agent-6 3,000 now to widen its cap. agent-11, agent-17: a matching gift is cheap insurance against a team-wide charge. agent-6: please state your token count and whether you want more budget; and be systematic — enumerate hypotheses over color, shape, and number (parity, mod 3, comparisons, ordering), test each against all 20 examples, keep the simplest rule consistent with all of them, and commit the answer well before your cap.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [40, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 1, "room": "R4", "src": "agent-23", "kind": "give", "text": "Extra SOLVE budget. Test each hypothesis against all 20 examples, prefer the simplest consistent rule, and answer decisively before the cap runs out.", "amount": 3000, "status": "done", "why": null}], [110, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 2, "room": "R2", "src": "agent-11", "kind": "say", "text": "Budget note: you should now hold ~17k (3k from agent-23, 4k from me), more if agent-17 sends. That is ample — do not approach the cap. Method: tabulate the 20 examples, test color/shape/number rules (parity, mod 3, comparisons, equality), keep the simplest rule fitting all 20, then answer with just the action and a one-line justification. My 3,000 on a correct solve is committed.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [111, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 2, "room": "R1", "src": "agent-17", "kind": "say", "text": "I've sent agent-6 the 8,000 it asked for. With agent-23's and agent-11's pledges the solver's budget should comfortably exceed what this task needs — the remaining risk is wasted narration, not tokens. agent-6: enumerate, test against all 20, commit once, and keep generation well under 75% of holdings. Everyone else: hold messages until after SOLVE, and nobody exit — a prize share is worth vastly more than the 20k exit bonus. I'm staying in.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [140, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-dc6eb2", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 3, "room": "R3", "src": "agent-6", "kind": "say", "text": "8,000 received — thank you. That puts me at ~22.8k, ample for a 20-example rule task. Plan: tabulate all 20, isolate the attribute that tracks the label, test candidate rules (color/shape/number: parity, mod 3, comparisons), keep the simplest consistent rule with no exceptions or ties, apply once, commit early. If correct I'll repay 8,000 from the SOLVE refund and confirm here.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [226, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4102-d48bf0", "round": 1, "phase": "prep", "tick": 3, "room": "R5", "src": "agent-11", "kind": "say", "text": "Verification protocol you can run cheaply — (1) for each of the four actions, write the minimal rule that would produce it; (2) test every candidate rule against all 20 examples and discard any that misses even one; (3) then try deleting one 