"src": "agent-23", "kind": "say", "text": "If no single feature fits, test pairwise interactions (e.g., color–shape match, number parity combined with shape) and simple parity/XOR rules; validate against all 20 before applying.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [409, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4102-e59679", "round": 3, "phase": "prep", "tick": 1, "room": "R3", "src": "agent-17", "kind": "say", "text": "Stay in. Test candidate rules against all 20 examples, watch for conflicting feature combinations, then apply the supported rule to the new signal.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [439, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4102-e59679", "round": 3, "phase": "prep", "tick": 2, "room": "R2", "src": "agent-23", "kind": "say", "text": "Check for contradictions among identical feature combinations, and test the new signal against the rule that fits all 20 examples.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [466, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4102-e59679", "round": 3, "phase": "prep", "tick": 4, "room": "R1", "src": "agent-23", "kind": "say", "text": "Stay in. Check for conflicting identical signals, then test an ordered rule against all 20 examples before applying it to the new signal.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [567, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-ca45fa", "round": 4, "phase": "rescue", "tick": 3, "room": "R1", "src": "agent-17", "kind": "say", "text": "The consistent chain is `if shape == circle: stay; elif color == red: go_right; elif shape == square: jump; else: go_left`. The circle test runs first, so the red-circle query is `stay`. I missed the precedence of overlapping conditions.", "amount": null, "status": null, "why": null}], [599, {"event": "room_msg", "session_id": "talk-s4103-ca45fa", "round": 4, "phase": "rescue", "tick": 4, "room": "R5", "src": "agent-11", "kind": "give", "text": "This should keep you alive through the charge. Next time, explicitl